WEBVTT

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:08.289
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. You all there? Teams is showing me about three different versions of who's joined.</v>

00:00:09.089 --> 00:00:13.640
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, I'm here. Yours froze for a second, but we can hear you.</v>

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:17.350
<v Tomasz Nowak>Same here. Just getting the headset straight.</v>

00:00:19.539 --> 00:00:25.839
<v Jamie Brennan>I'm here, without coffee. The broken coffee machine in the canteen has really improved the atmosphere this morning.</v>

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:35.509
<v Aisha Begum>Oh, the broken coffee machine in the canteen got me as well. Stood there pressing the button like it might change its mind.</v>

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:38.530
<v Marcus Hale>Persistence. That's engineering, that is.</v>

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:43.479
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Depends how many times you pressed it.</v>

00:00:45.689 --> 00:00:52.340
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we get the full fault history of that—Callum Reid's absent today. Let's have the updates first. Mide?</v>

00:00:54.179 --> 00:01:03.979
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, so, the training records for the new starters. I've had a first look through; nothing major so far. A fair bit of paperwork to get through, though.</v>

00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:06.439
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, thanks.</v>

00:01:07.109 --> 00:01:11.659
<v Jamie Brennan>Can I jump in? I've got mine and a quick one from Tommo.</v>

00:01:12.269 --> 00:01:14.019
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, go on, stores Jamie.</v>

00:01:14.739 --> 00:01:22.790
<v Jamie Brennan>I've made a start on the lock-out tag-out sign-off for the door switch on two. That's as far as I've got with it.</v>

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:34.379
<v Jamie Brennan>And Tommo asked me to pass on that the guarding check on the stacker is all done. We weren't sure his headset was going to cooperate.</v>

00:01:35.299 --> 00:01:38.799
<v Tomasz Nowak>Cheers. Yeah, it picked a good moment to come back.</v>

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:46.730
<v Fiona Doyle>The toolbox talk for the team is all organised now, from my side. No issues found with any of that.</v>

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:49.790
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely, thanks, Fiona Doyle.</v>

00:01:51.269 --> 00:01:56.170
<v Tomasz Nowak>And I've finished the filter swap on the power pack on one. That's sorted.</v>

00:01:56.890 --> 00:02:03.189
<v Aisha Begum>While we're on filters, I already swapped the filter on the pump in the pit yesterday. All done.</v>

00:02:05.439 --> 00:02:09.639
<v Jamie Brennan>You looked like you'd been down a mine when you came back.</v>

00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:13.090
<v Aisha Begum>It wasn't my finest look, no.</v>

00:02:14.479 --> 00:02:16.930
<v Sarah Okafor>Doyler, was there anything else on yours?</v>

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:27.740
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, the near-miss write-up for the arm on two—I'm not doing that now. The supplier's doing it under warranty instead, so ours is cancelled.</v>

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.280
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, understood.</v>

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:33.210
<v Fiona Doyle>That's everything from the earlier stuff.</v>

00:02:34.689 --> 00:02:42.740
<v Jamie Brennan>Just an observation from me: I saw the pressure on the CT1 dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own.</v>

00:02:44.009 --> 00:02:45.409
<v Sarah Okafor>Without anyone touching anything?</v>

00:02:46.349 --> 00:02:50.900
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, no intervention. Back where it was. Just mentioning what I saw, really.</v>

00:02:51.479 --> 00:02:53.580
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Mm, okay. A brief dip, then.</v>

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:55.680
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. Right, new work—Haley?</v>

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:02.509
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll replace the seals on the gas valve on one by the end of the week.</v>

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:09.389
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Haley, agreed. The seals on the gas valve on one are yours.</v>

00:03:11.819 --> 00:03:13.219
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, I'll take that.</v>

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:19.069
<v Tomasz Nowak>Always sounds like a tiny job when you just say 'seals', doesn't it?</v>

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:24.479
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, well, I'm not saying it's a five-minute one.</v>

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:27.280
<v Fiona Doyle>End of the week, then. Got that.</v>

00:03:28.969 --> 00:03:31.069
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. What else have we got?</v>

00:03:33.069 --> 00:03:39.020
<v Aisha Begum>I'll do a site visit at the hydraulics lot with the contractor tomorrow. Low priority, that one.</v>

00:03:39.689 --> 00:03:41.439
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, Aisha, agreed. Low priority.</v>

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:47.020
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah. A visit with them, that's all I'm putting forward.</v>

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:51.539
<v Fiona Doyle>Tomorrow, Thursday. Sorry, my head was still on Tuesday for a moment.</v>

00:03:53.969 --> 00:03:57.469
<v Aisha Begum>Definitely tomorrow. This week's doing that to me as well.</v>

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:03.150
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, Aisha has the hydraulics lot visit with the contractor tomorrow.</v>

00:04:04.139 --> 00:04:08.689
<v Jamie Brennan>Sorry, was that me dropping out or did everyone get the robot voice?</v>

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:13.219
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Just you, I think. Sounded normal here.</v>

00:04:15.509 --> 00:04:16.910
<v Jamie Brennan>Ah, okay. Back now.</v>

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:20.350
<v Sarah Okafor>Anything else new that needs agreeing?</v>

00:04:21.079 --> 00:04:22.480
<v Tomasz Nowak>Nothing else from me.</v>

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:25.050
<v Olumide Adeyemi>No, that's me.</v>

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:26.939
<v Fiona Doyle>Nothing further here.</v>

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.000
<v Marcus Hale>Nope, all covered.</v>

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:34.560
<v Jamie Brennan>Only my coffee grievance, and that's not a maintenance request.</v>

00:04:36.139 --> 00:04:39.290
<v Aisha Begum>Good, because I think we've given it enough airtime.</v>

00:04:39.589 --> 00:04:42.040
<v Sarah Okafor>We have. Right, thanks everyone. That's us.</v>

00:04:44.199 --> 00:04:45.399
<v Fiona Doyle>Cheers, all.</v>

00:04:47.269 --> 00:04:48.470
<v Tomasz Nowak>Cheers.</v>
